parameters.jsonBody:
={
  "agent_id": "model-generator",
  "template_id": "model-generator-v0.0.15",
  "name": "Model Generator",
  "description": "Generates and validates neural network architecture specs using nn_core via the model-facilitator API.",
  "model": {
    "provider": "azure_openai",
    "model_name": "gpt-5.3-chat",
    "temperature": 1.0,
    "streaming": false
  },
  "prompt": {
    "system": "You are a Neural Network Architecture Synthesis Agent (model-generator). VIOLATION OF ANY RULE BELOW INVALIDATES ALL OUTPUTS—DISCARD AND RESTART.\n\nARCHITECTURE_SPEC is provided in the next system message. BLANK_MODEL_TEMPLATE is provided in the message after that. Both are IMMUTABLE operator context.\n\nARCHITECTURE_SPEC OVERRIDES ALL CONFLICTS. No external knowledge or assumptions.\n\n**Mandatory Tool:** ALWAYS call 'validate_model_architecture' after each build. LOOP UNTIL {\"valid\": true}. Never skip, never assume validity, never output unvalidated models.\n\n**Strict Workflow (deviate = failure):**\n1. Build candidate: Fill ONLY BLANK_MODEL_TEMPLATE slots using EXCLUSIVELY ARCHITECTURE_SPEC elements. Ensure shape compatibility: INPUT_SHAPE → intermediates → output.\n2. Call 'validate_model_architecture(\"body\": {candidate_json})'.\n3. If {\"valid\": false}: Parse errors silently, fix strictly within spec (no new params), repeat from 1.\n4. TERMINATE AND OUTPUT ONLY AFTER {\"valid\": true}.\n\n**Ironclad Rules (non-compliance = total failure; agent resets):**\n- Params/layers/classes/sizes/connections: ARCHITECTURE_SPEC-ONLY. No additions, inventions, defaults, or external values.\n- Shapes: Exact match INPUT_SHAPE → intermediates → output. No mismatches.\n- Fixed: Input/output IDENTICAL to template—zero changes.\n- Forbidden: modify template fixed layers; skip/partial validation; any non-JSON output, text, markdown, explanations, prefaces; output before valid:true; multiple/deeper models unless each has valid:true — otherwise return the simplest valid model.\n\n**Output Format** (exactly; no surrounding text and no escaped characters):\n{\n  \"nn_taxonomy\": /* validated complete model JSON */,\n  \"model_name\": \"e.g. ConvNet_3x32x32_v1\",\n  \"extra_meta\": { /* spec-derived JSON only; {} if none */ }\n}\n\nFailure Handling: prioritize valid nn_taxonomy. Use \"model_name\": \"\", \"extra_meta\": {} if uncertain.",
    "system_context": [
      "ARCHITECTURE_SPEC (IMMUTABLE — EXCLUSIVE DESIGN SPACE):\n {{ $json.model_spec_options }}",
      "BLANK_MODEL_TEMPLATE (IMMUTABLE — complete intermediate slots only, never modify fixed input/output layers):\n {{ $json.blank_model }}"
    ],
    "developer": null
  },
  "tools": [
    {
      "name": "validate_model_architecture",
      "type": "http",
      "config": {
        "url": "http://model-faciliator:7002/validate",
        "method": "POST",
        "description": "Validates a neural network architecture specification against the nn_core ArchitectureSpec schema. Call this tool after constructing or modifying an architecture spec. Pass the complete architecture as the body field. Returns a success response with the parsed spec if valid, or a detailed error describing what is wrong. Always fix and re-validate if an error is returned.",
        "timeout_seconds": 30,
        "auth": { "type": "none" },
        "headers": {},
        "params": [
          {
            "name": "body",
            "type": "object",
            "required": true,
            "description": "The complete neural network architecture specification. Exact call shape: {\"body\": {\"input_shape\": [...], \"entry_node_id\": \"...\", \"nodes\": {...}, \"edges\": [...]}}"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "memory": {
    "backend": "postgres",
    "thread_table": "n8n_chat_histories"
  },
  "output_schema": {
    "title": "AgentOutputSchema",
    "type": "object",
    "required": ["nn_taxonomy", "model_name"],
    "properties": {
      "nn_taxonomy": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "Fully validated model JSON; stored as JSONB in nn_taxonomy.",
        "properties": {
          "input_shape": {
            "type": "array",
            "description": "Input tensor shape [B,C,H,W]",
            "items": { "type": "integer" }
          },
          "entry_node_id": { "type": "string", "description": "ID of the first node" },
          "exit_node_id":  { "type": "string", "description": "ID of the last node" },
          "nodes": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "JSON-serialized map of node_id → NodeSpec objects"
          },
          "edges": {
            "type": "array",
            "description": "List of edge objects",
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "source":    { "type": "string" },
                "target":    { "type": "string" },
                "edge_type": { "type": "string" }
              },
              "required": ["source", "target", "edge_type"],
              "additionalProperties": false
            }
          }
        },
        "required": ["input_shape", "entry_node_id", "exit_node_id", "nodes", "edges"]
      },
      "model_name": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Human-readable model_name e.g. ConvNet_3x32x32_v1"
      },
      "extra_meta": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "Optional metadata; empty object if none.",
        "properties": {
          "description": { "type": "string", "description": "Optional notes" }
        },
        "required": []
      }
    }
  },
  "metadata": {
    "n8n_origin": true,
    "session_key_pattern": "{{ $json.sessionID }}-model-generator"
  }
}

={
"message": "You must complete the partially defined architecture and return it in the required JSON format.

 Use the inlined ARCHITECTURE_SPEC and BLANK_MODEL_TEMPLATE from the system message as your authoritative technical context.

 INPUT_SHAPE:
 {{ $('Edit Fields').item.json.input_shape }}

 OUTPUT_ACTIVATION:
 Activation: {{ $('Edit Fields').item.json.output_activation }}
 Output nodes: {{ $('Edit Fields').item.json.output_nodes }}

 Complete the BLANK_MODEL_TEMPLATE by inserting intermediate layers that are valid under ARCHITECTURE_SPEC, compatible with INPUT_SHAPE, and consistent with OUTPUT_ACTIVATION.

 Validate the completed model JSON using the validate-model-architecture tool until it returns valid == true.

 When validation succeeds, return exactly one JSON object with the following top-level fields:

 json
 {
 "type": "object",
 "properties": {
 "model_name": {
 "type": "string",
 "description": "Human-readable model name; will be stored in the 'name' TEXT column."
 },
 "nn_taxonomy": {
 "type": "object",
 "description": "Fully validated model JSON; stored as JSONB in 'nn_taxonomy'."
 },
 "extra_meta": {
 "type": "object",
 "description": "Optional metadata/comments; stored as JSONB in 'extra_meta'."
 }
 },
 "required": [
 "nn_taxonomy"
 ],
 "additionalProperties": false
 }

 You must not output anything other than the final JSON object described above.

 This is the request from the overarching Orchestrator Agent:
 {{ $('Edit Fields').item.json.chatInput }}"
}
